<Article title="Account & Pro Terms | DeadHangs" description="How DeadHangs accounts, optional Pro subscriptions, cancellation and your saved training data work." h1="Account and Pro terms." subtitle="The free tools stay free. You choose whether to store your log online." crumbs={[{name:'Account terms'}]} noindex>
  <div class="article-body">
    <p>Updated 8 November 2026. DeadHangs is operated by ND Media Ltd. For account support, billing questions or a cancellation request, email <a href="mailto:hello@sunnypatel.co.uk">hello@sunnypatel.co.uk</a>.</p>
    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <p>Creating an account with Google is free. Use your own account and keep access to it secure. Signing in does not upload your existing training entries. Check the entries on a shared device before choosing to sync them.</p>
    <h2>What Pro includes</h2>
    <p>DeadHangs Pro provides cloud storage, deliberate sync between devices and progress history from your recorded training entries. The account page shows the storage limit before an upload. Your timer settings and saved training goal remain on the device. An internet connection and a supported browser with JavaScript are required for account features.</p>
    <p>The timer, local log, local progress tools and calculators remain free. Pro is software for recording your own training. It does not include coaching, medical advice or a promise of physical results.</p>
    <h2>Subscription and renewal</h2>
    <p>The launch plans are £4.99 per month or £39 per year, billed in GBP. Checkout is available only when payment setup is ready. Review the final total, billing interval and seller information in checkout before paying. A subscription renews at the selected interval until you cancel renewal; there is no free trial.</p>
    <p>After a successful payment, Pro activates when the payment provider confirms the subscription. If checkout completes but your account does not update, refresh the account page or contact support. Do not pay a second time.</p>
    <h2>Cancel, export or delete</h2>
    <p>Choose Manage billing in your account to cancel renewal through Stripe. Pro normally continues until the end of the paid period. You can also email us to cancel, including the email used for your account. You do not need to give a reason.</p>
    <p>Your right to cancel during any applicable cooling-off period, receive a refund required by law or seek a remedy for a faulty service is unaffected. Contact us to exercise those rights. Cancelling renewal through the billing portal does not itself request a refund.</p>
    <p>After Pro ends, you can export or delete the cloud log. Further cloud uploads require an active Pro subscription. Export a copy before deleting your account. Account deletion immediately stops any continuing subscription and removes your account and cloud log; access to the deleted account cannot be restored. Local entries on your devices are managed separately.</p>
    <h2>Your data and availability</h2>
    <p>You remain responsible for the accuracy of entries you record. Keep an exported backup of records you want to retain. The service may occasionally be unavailable for maintenance or a provider outage. The <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> explains what we store and how to request access, correction or deletion.</p>
    <p>We may restrict access where necessary to address abuse or protect other users. Nothing here excludes rights or liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>
  </div>
</Article>
